# Files that Linux must execute have to keep LF endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so without these
# rules git rewrites them to CRLF on checkout. A CRLF shebang makes Linux report
# "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" - and the Docker build copies these
# straight out of the Windows working tree, so the container runner would break on
# a fresh clone while working fine on the machine that wrote it.
*.sh text eol=lf
scripts/runner/Dockerfile text eol=lf
